# An ALLOW-LIST, inverted: ignore everything, then un-ignore the handful of paths that are
# genuinely meant to land in somebody's home directory.
#
# WHY NOT A DENY-LIST: it was one, and it leaked. `debug-worker/` and `uninstall.sh` were
# added to the repo weeks apart, neither was on the list, and chezmoi was placing
# ~/debug-worker/wrangler.toml and ~/uninstall.sh into a stranger's home. A deny-list makes
# the DEFAULT "copy it into their home", and the default is what you get on the day nobody
# remembers to add a line.
#
# ⚠ THESE PATTERNS MATCH THE TARGET NAME, NOT THE SOURCE NAME. `dot_claude/**` matches
# nothing; the target is `.claude/**`. Writing the source name here silently places NOTHING
# — which is how the first version of this file dropped every skill and both settings files
# while looking correct.
*
!.claude
!.claude/**
!.mwk-shell.sh
!bin
!bin/mwk
!.chezmoiscripts
!.chezmoiscripts/**
# The howto, placed ONCE (create_) as the root README of ~/mwk-work — so it renders at
# http://127.0.0.1:29200/ — and never overwritten: ours on day one, theirs after. Nothing
# else under ~/mwk-work, and nothing under ~/projects, is chezmoi's to see.
!mwk-work
!mwk-work/README.md
